s":"saying/like"}],"gloss":"clearly"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நோவாதோன்","parts":[{"text":"நோவாதோன்","lemma":"நோவாதோன்","gloss":"he who does not feel pain"}],"gloss":"he who does not feel pain"},{"surface":"வயின்","parts":[{"text":"வயின்","lemma":"வயின்","gloss":"towards"}],"gloss":"towards"},{"surface":"திரங்கி","parts":[{"text":"திரங்கி","lemma":"திரங்கு","gloss":"having withered"}],"gloss":"having withered"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வாயா","parts":[{"text":"வாயா","lemma":"வாயா","gloss":"not ripening"}],"gloss":"not ripening"},{"surface":"வன்கனிக்கு","parts":[{"text":"வன்கனிக்கு","lemma":"வன்கனிக்கு","gloss":"for the hard fruit"}],"gloss":"for the hard fruit","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"உலமருவோரே","parts":[{"text":"உலமருவோர்","lemma":"உலமருவோர்","gloss":"those who wander"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"indeed those who wander"}]}],"literal":"Rise now, O heart! Let us go, who are we? / Without the desire that is like drinking, ruined / even after seeing us nearby, acting like they do not know, / without the heart rejoicing, with a fallen face, a ruined gift / those without effort will not desire, they are not / saying 'come' is needed for those of worthy rank. / Big indeed is the world, those who cherish are many indeed! / Like a fierce, strong yali, / the mind, without its inner fire being extinguished and subdued, clearly / towards him who does not feel pain, pining / are those who wander for the hard fruit that does not ripen.","translation":"Rise now, my heart! Let us go. Who are we to stay here? Without that eager desire that is like drinking us in, acting as if they do not know us even when seeing us nearby, offering a diminished gift with a fallen face, without a rejoicing heart—even those who lack effort would not desire such a gift; we are not such people. For those of worthy rank, a welcoming 'Come!' is what is needed. The world is vast, and those who cherish us are many! Like a fierce and powerful yali, our mind will not let its inner fire be extinguished and subdued. Only those who pine and wither before a man who feels no pity are like those who wander in vain around a hard, unripened fruit.","modern":"என் நெஞ்சமே! இப்போது எழுந்து போவோம். நாம் யார் இங்கே இருக்க? நம்மைப் பருகிவிடுவது போன்ற ஆவலோடு வரவேற்காமல், அருகில் பார்த்தும் பார்க்காதவர் போல நடித்து, மனம் மகிழாமல், முகம் சோர்ந்து தரும் இழிவான பரிசிலை, முயற்சி இல்லாத சோம்பேறிகள் கூட விரும்ப மாட்டார்கள்; நாம் அப்படிப்பட்டவர்கள் அல்லர். தகுதியுடையவர்களுக்கு 'வருக' என்று இன்முகத்தோடு அழைப்பதே வேண்டும். உலகம் மிகப் பெரியது; நம்மைப் பேணிப் பாதுகாப்பவர்கள் பலர் இருக்கிறார்கள். வலிமை மிக்க யாளி மிருகத்தைப் போல, நம் நெஞ்சம் தன் உள்ளத்து மானத்தை இழந்து அடங்கிவிடாது. இரக்கமில்லாதவனிடம் போய் வாடி நிற்பவர்கள், ஒருபோதும் பழுக்காத வன்மையான காய்க்காகக் காத்துக் கிடந்து அலையும் அறிவிலிகள் ஆவர்.","explanation":"This poem is composed by Peruñcitiraṉār, addressed to Iḷaveḷimāṉ, under the tiṇai pāṭāṇ and tuṟai paricil. The poet had visited the chieftain Iḷaveḷimāṉ seeking patronage, but the chieftain treated him coldly, offering a meager gift without a warm welcome. Offended by this disrespectful treatment, the poet addresses his own heart, declaring that they must leave immediately. He asserts that self-respecting scholars and poets do not value gifts given without joy and respect; even those without any drive would reject such a cold offering. He compares the unfeeling patron to a hard, unripened fruit that can never satisfy anyone's hunger, and compares those who wait on such patrons to foolish wanderers wasting their time. The poet proudly proclaims that the world is vast and filled with generous patrons who know how to honor worthy people, and compares his own unyielding spirit to a fierce, powerful yali.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.1],[1.1,1.6],[1.6,1.7],[1.7,2.5],[2.5,2.5],[2.5,2.9],[2.9,3.6],[3.6,4.6],[4.6,4.6],[4.6,5.1],[5.1,5.6],[5.6,6.5],[6.6,6.7],[6.7,6.9],[6.9,7.88],[7.88,8.36],[8.36,8.36],[8.36,9.8],[9.8,